From u3a775dfa0a96bf95 at groups.google.com  Fri May 27 14:46:55 2011
From: u3a775dfa0a96bf95 at groups.google.com (Stavros Macrakis)
Date: Fri, 27 May 2011 14:46:55 +0000
Subject: Re: ddply and POSIXlt
Message-ID: <5amu5_LdyK8.8HaJi7mcwToJ@manipulatr.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <5amu5_LdyK8.TNHkKJJnvQoJ@manipulatr.groups.google.com>
References: <5amu5_LdyK8.tPXAVWDQ75EJ@manipulatr.groups.google.com> <5amu5_LdyK8.TNHkKJJnvQoJ@manipulatr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/manipulatr/c/5amu5_LdyK8/m/8HaJi7mcwToJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The fundamental problem is that POSIXlt and POSIXct values are not actually "objects" in the object-oriented programming sense -- that is, defined only by the operations that are meaningful on them -- the underlying representation "leaks out".  This is a problem with base (S3) R itself, where method dispatching is often (but not always) supported, but abstraction through information hiding is not.  There are better object systems available, but much of R is S3-based.

               -s

